
<section class="my-8 rounded-[32px] border-2 border-orange-100
                bg-gradient-to-b from-white via-orange-50/20 to-slate-50/50
                p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">

  <header class="mb-7 border-b-2 border-orange-100 pb-5">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
      <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl
                  border border-orange-200 bg-orange-100 text-2xl">
        🧭
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-800">
          Investigation workflow
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
          Understand the difference between collecting information, evaluating
          evidence, completing research, and preserving the investigation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">

    <article class="rounded-[26px] border-2 border-orange-100 bg-white p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-orange-100 text-xl">01</span>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-800">Define the question</h3>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Explain what needs to be understood, why the question matters, and
        what would count as a satisfactory answer. Separate the research
        objective from assumptions that still need verification.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-[26px] border-2 border-sky-100 bg-white p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-sky-100 text-xl">02</span>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-800">Collect evidence</h3>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Preserve source details, dates, and the claims supported by each
        source. Distinguish original evidence from summaries and interpretations.
        Record conflicting findings instead of hiding them.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-[26px] border-2 border-violet-100 bg-white p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-violet-100 text-xl">03</span>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-800">Review conclusions</h3>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Use annotations to explain significance, uncertainty, and reviewer
        decisions. Check whether the available evidence supports each conclusion
        and identify unresolved questions before completion.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-[26px] border-2 border-emerald-100 bg-white p-5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="flex h-11 w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-emerald-100 text-xl">04</span>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-800">Preserve and improve</h3>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Save snapshots at meaningful milestones, document important changes,
        and reopen completed research when new information justifies another
        review. Retain the reasoning behind important decisions.
      </p>
    </article>

  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border-2 border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5">
    <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-amber-900">
      Research quality principle
    </h3>

    <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-7 text-amber-900">
      A completed investigation is a workflow state, not proof that its
      conclusions are correct. Confidence should reflect the quality,
      relevance, independence, and limitations of the evidence.
    </p>
  </div>

</section>